# Framework-managed transient state — uncommitted by design.
# The build session's in-flight checkpoint log (see STAGE-PROMPT-PROTOCOL
# <status_log>). Read by an orchestrator consultation; cleared at stage close.
.claude/build-status.md

# The session's current role (work / verifier / orchestrator / refactor). Local to
# the machine; not part of the project's shared state. `.claude/role` is the ONLY
# marker written or read — its compatibility alias was retired. The retired name stays
# listed below on purpose: nothing writes it any more, but a project that predates the
# removal can still have one on disk, and it must never be committable.
.claude/role
.claude/active-mode

# PROC-001 red-gate markers (shipped via the red-gate hook): the open-stage marker,
# the role recorded at open, and the per-stage red-approval marker. Per-session, never
# committed. Comments stay on their OWN lines — an inline `#` becomes part of the
# pattern and ignores nothing.
.claude/stage-active
.claude/stage-role
.claude/red-approved
# M33.F the stage views (scripts/stage-view.cjs): generated read surfaces, rebuilt from HEAD,
# never committed.
.claude/views/

# The last lane summaries verify-local writes per run (fast / stage / release). Read
# by `--reconcile` at closeout; local run state, never committed.
.claude/verify-last-*.json
# One line per lane run (M33.G): the stage's measure line counts them.
.claude/verify-last-runs.jsonl

# Build-receipt event ledgers (per-session JSONL written by the receipts
# machinery; local observability data, never committed).
.claude/receipts/
# M30.H the terminal channel: the two logs (.claude/channel/*.jsonl) are TRACKED and committed
# with the stage - never ignore them. Only the transient per-session state is ignored.
.claude/channel/cursor.*
.claude/channel/turn
.claude/channel/watch.*.json
.claude/channel/send-token
.claude/channel/outgoing.md
.claude/channel/present.*.json
.claude/channel/approval.json

# Build-receipt reports (rendered JSON/HTML/MD views written by
# `node scripts/build-receipts.cjs render`; local observability output). This
# entry is a default, not a wall — a report you want to keep is deliberately
# trackable: negate or delete this line for the files you commit.
reports/

# The installer and its download / state folder (sbak-install's own files). The installer is a
# release asset you can download again, and the state folder stays in place after a failed
# install; neither belongs in the project's history. Root-anchored on purpose.
/sbak-install.cjs
/sbak-install.cjs.sha256
/.sbak-install/

